    "Teacher slips / vs book: (1) 0:10:21 «جبکہ صاحبین کہتے ہیں کہ… تزکیہ… گواہی ہی کی طرح» — the two-muzakki view is Imam Muhammad's alone (matn v5 409: «وهذا عند أبي حنيفة وأبي يوسف… وقال محمد: لا يجوز إلا اثنان»); he himself said Abu Hanifa + Abu Yusuf at 0:10:00/0:10:47 and Muhammad at 0:11:21. Card 3 attributes it to Muhammad. (2) 0:07:15–0:07:40: he says the muzakki should also say 'آزاد' («بہتر یہ ہے»); the book gives that as one قيل and then «وقيل: يكتفي بقوله: هو عدل… وهذا أصح» (v5 409). Card 2 gives both and marks the book's أصح. (3) 0:33:14/0:33:34: he frames the exception as 'adult slaves have a hand over themselves, so no testimony; small ones if known to be slaves'; the book's split is: known to be رقيق → may testify (any age; «لأن الرقيق لا يكون في يد نفسه»); not known but too small to speak → may; grown (يعبران عن أنفسهما, النهاية) and not known → the exception. Card 7 states his version and the book's split separately. (4) 0:29:28: his burial example (saw a burial, people told him who died) is framed as hearsay; the book's point (v5 415) is that attending the burial or praying the janaza is itself معاينة and is accepted even if he explains it to the qadi. Card 6 gives both. (5) 0:26:53 adds police chief / administrative post to ولاية القاضي — his extension, not in the matn; card 6 faida marks it as استاد. (9) 0:09:36 «تو پھر گویا تزکیہ ہو گیا اور اب گواہوں پر فیصلہ کیا جائے گا» — he says this of «عادل ہیں مگر غلط فہمی ہوئی», but under the zahir position (matn v5 409) the khasm's tazkiya is not accepted at all; it holds only on the Abu Yusuf/Muhammad riwaya (with Muhammad adding a second vetter). Card 3 line 3 no longer carries that stamp. (10) 0:22:41–0:23:02 he applies «ولا كذلك الشهادة في الصك» to the qadi; the footnote (الكفاية ٤٦٥/٦-٤٦٦) reads it of the witness finding his testimony in a صك held by another; card 5 states the footnote's reading and keeps his qadi example as his. (11) 0:13:22 «صرف یہ ضروری ہے کہ اس کے اندر عقل ہو» — he says «مثلاً» at 0:13:37; card uses «مثلاً» (sight at tahammul also matters, cf. v5 419 الأعمى). (6) 0:25:07 «اب زید جا کے گواہی دیتا ہے» — Zaid is the husband in his own example; slip of name for the witness; card avoids it. (7) 0:20:08–0:20:30 the diary example has the witness hearing a divorce in Peshawar; fine. (8) 0:14:04 nikah-form example and 0:12:58 kafir example (tahammul vs ada; only عقل at tahammul) are his own, not on these pages; carded as استاد.",
